decision: pass
reviewer: claude-opus-5-5 (self-review)
audience: Technical leads and maintainers
purpose: How is a hook copy reported when there is no baseline record to compare against?

Records the addition of the unrecorded hook state for copies that differ from the template without a baseline record, refining the verdict of ADR 0015.
Translated from Korean to English as a frozen record; the 2026-09-10 Windows re-verification incident, commit b955c49 and the three rejected alternatives are preserved.
Headings mapped to Decision / Context and constraints / Rationale and alternatives / Consequences; the reference to ADR 0015's 「영향」 section is rendered as its Consequences section.
Korean literals kept at lines 34 and 40: the hooks status message was actual Korean CLI output (lib/adoption.sh at that time), so it stays in backticks with an English gloss.
The lead's paraphrase of the new message is translated as prose, since it is not a verbatim CLI string.

